  "known_limitations": [
    "All API responses were retrieved on 2026-11-27, after the claimed snapshots. They do not recover the contemporaneous response or its latency/revision state.",
    "No exchangeDataDelayedBy field was returned. Yahoo official coverage lists Nasdaq as real-time, but that generic statement does not establish the latency of the old capture. No 15-minute shift was assumed.",
    "meta.previousClose, regularMarketPrice and regularMarketTime describe the latest quote and do not necessarily refer to the requested historical date. Historical denominators come from the separately audited daily data.",
    "volume is deliberately excluded from this compact comparison: the 1m response contains anomalously large individual values. For 2026-11-16 the direct regular-session sum is 2,620,662,976 shares, versus 333,822,062 in the audited daily dataset. No undocumented repair or cumulative-volume reconstruction was performed.",
    "Premarket and postmarket volume fields are zero in these responses; this was not interpreted as absence of trading.",
    "The 2026-11-25 request uses UTC day boundaries and also includes the last hour of 2026-11-24 postmarket. Each comparison row was selected by exact timestamp and historical session, not merely the response filename.",
    "F-099 160.40 matches the 13:41 UTC Close, one minute before the archived 13:42 label. This is a useful comparison, not proof of how the old snapshot was sampled."
  ],
